Found while working k100. The OpenAI message list request_to_openai builds can contain consecutive user messages: the tool-images user message followed by the client text of the same Anthropic message (existing), and since k100 a standalone <system-reminder> user message after a run of tool messages. Templates with strict role alternation (Gemma) may refuse that, depending on how they render tool messages. k100 removed the mid-conversation system role, not same-role neighbours. Done: decide whether Skeid merges adjacent user messages (content arrays included) on the Anthropic face, without changing the prompt prefix of earlier turns; test on the forwarded OpenAI messages.
